From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sf2000_linux <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 06:35:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: skip EBase WG probing on SF2000

The HC15xx/SF2000 bring-up intentionally treats the CPU as MIPS32r1 first.
Some devices may expose pieces of later MIPS revisions, and QEMU's 24K model
does, but the early EBase.WG probe writes CP0 EBase while temporarily changing
BEV. That is not needed for this single-core board and it can stall before the
first post-entry diagnostic marker.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -737,7 +737,7 @@ static void decode_configs(struct cpuinfo_mips *c)
 	}
 
 	/* Probe the EBase.WG bit */
-	if (cpu_has_mips_r2_r6) {
+	if (cpu_has_mips_r2_r6 && !IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000)) {
 		u64 ebase;
 		unsigned int status;
 
-- 
